Round-2 findings and decisions needed

1. The full old launch command still appears (R1-2 reopened, P2)
The mixed-policy deletion from round 1 is fixed. The replacement now recognizes
only a narrow standalone command form. It misses the original command's report
and status arguments.
Concrete input:
  claude -p --model opus --dangerously-skip-permissions "/adv-review-loop
  <branch> firstmate report=$REPORT status=<absolute status path>"
This is one physical command line in the tested configuration.
Wrong result: both the generated ship brief and promoted-scout instructions
retain that raw command instead of replacing it with a launcher pointer.
Likelihood: certain for that existing full command form. Generated instructions
do state that the bundled launcher takes precedence, so a wrong-runtime launch
depends on a worker following the retained command. No real wrong-runtime call
was made in this reproduction. The remaining ambiguity defeats the requested
removal of hand-built launches and can again tempt a worker into the old path.
Who it affects: workers using that configured review step, and firstmate when
they need another launch attempt or wait on the wrong runtime.
Fix cost: roughly 10-20 minutes for a regression and support for the full known
standalone command, while preserving policy prose and compound instructions.
Structural option: stop growing an ad hoc command whitelist; use a structured
launch-template slot or parse the standalone launch command while preserving
all surrounding policy. Estimated 25-45 minutes, plus compatibility tests.
This is the second correction in the same area, so firstmate should see and
choose the structural option before another fix round proceeds.

2. A success result followed by an error can pass (R2-1, new P2)
Concrete fake Claude stdout consists of two JSON objects:
  {"type":"result","is_error":false,"result":"real role reply"}
  {"type":"result","is_error":true,"result":"failed"}
The process exits successfully. The launcher returns success for both roles,
extracting the first reply and silently filtering out the later error.
The CLI's JSON format is a single result, so this malformed multi-result stream
should be rejected as an invalid receipt.
Likelihood: proved with deterministic fakes; the frequency in real Claude output
is unmeasured. This concerns the Claude path selected after the dated Codex rule
expires. It affects any worker receiving such malformed output and could let an
incomplete or failed review/fix be treated as complete.
Fix cost: roughly 5-15 minutes to require exactly one valid result object and
add success-plus-error and other multi-result regressions for both Claude roles.
No new coordinating state is needed; stricter receipt validation is sufficient.

